WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.199 --> 00:00:03.439
Now, before we go further,

2
00:00:03.439 --> 00:00:06.219
I want to talk about our player controller

3
00:00:06.219 --> 00:00:08.019
because we're going to actually be creating

4
00:00:08.019 --> 00:00:09.539
a brand new player controller

5
00:00:09.539 --> 00:00:12.800
for this interaction logic to go into.

6
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:15.839
And the reason for this is because we want the player,

7
00:00:15.839 --> 00:00:18.260
no matter if it's a player or a car

8
00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:19.859
or a spaceship or a ball,

9
00:00:19.859 --> 00:00:23.980
to be able to press the E key on their keyboard

10
00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:27.059
and be able to interact with this light switch.

11
00:00:27.059 --> 00:00:30.780
And this is a really key importance

12
00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:32.500
of building things inside of Unreal.

13
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:34.100
We always want to make sure that we build stuff

14
00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.179
in the correct location.

15
00:00:35.179 --> 00:00:37.679
Now we could build all of this functionality

16
00:00:37.679 --> 00:00:40.420
that we're building in each one of these classes.

17
00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:42.259
We could build it inside of our player,

18
00:00:42.259 --> 00:00:44.539
inside of our car, inside of our spaceship

19
00:00:44.539 --> 00:00:46.420
or inside of our ball.

20
00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:48.820
But that means that there are now four locations

21
00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:50.899
where we need to maintain our code.

22
00:00:50.899 --> 00:00:55.340
Since the player controller acts as a way

23
00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:57.740
to take different pawns over,

24
00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:01.000
while still giving the user the same type of input

25
00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:02.859
based off the device they're using,

26
00:01:02.859 --> 00:01:07.239
we can input code or implement code

27
00:01:07.239 --> 00:01:09.079
inside of our player controller

28
00:01:09.079 --> 00:01:12.599
and have that accessible to the user

29
00:01:12.599 --> 00:01:15.719
no matter the type of pawn that they are.

30
00:01:15.719 --> 00:01:17.000
So let's go ahead and pop over here

31
00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:18.040
to the editor really quick.

32
00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:19.760
And I'm gonna hit control space

33
00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:21.980
and we're going to right click inside of here.

34
00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:23.519
We're gonna go to our blueprint class.

35
00:01:23.519 --> 00:01:25.540
And then from our pick parent class,

36
00:01:26.219 --> 00:01:27.640
we're gonna look for our player controller.

37
00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:30.180
I'm gonna call this BP underscore

38
00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:35.629
interaction, interaction controller.

39
00:01:35.629 --> 00:01:38.150
Let's go ahead and double click on it to open it up.

40
00:01:38.150 --> 00:01:41.349
Now to understand what we're gonna do next,

41
00:01:41.349 --> 00:01:43.909
let's take a look at the following image.

42
00:01:43.909 --> 00:01:45.409
So what we're gonna be doing

43
00:01:45.409 --> 00:01:49.629
is we are going to be creating a line in space.

44
00:01:49.629 --> 00:01:51.590
And that line is going to start

45
00:01:51.590 --> 00:01:52.989
in the center of our character.

46
00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:56.590
And it's gonna go out at X distance that we define.

47
00:01:56.590 --> 00:02:02.659
And anything that is inside of that line,

48
00:02:02.659 --> 00:02:05.140
we can determine different properties about it.

49
00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:06.939
And for us, what we're gonna be doing

50
00:02:06.939 --> 00:02:09.500
is we're gonna be casting this line

51
00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:10.879
X unit out into space.

52
00:02:10.879 --> 00:02:13.900
And we're gonna see if that line comes in contact

53
00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:16.699
with an object that contains our interface.

54
00:02:16.699 --> 00:02:17.819
And if it does,

55
00:02:17.819 --> 00:02:20.039
then we'll be able to do something with it.

56
00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:21.780
So again, this is an example here,

57
00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:24.699
a visual example of what we're gonna be creating.

58
00:02:24.699 --> 00:02:29.960
We're gonna be creating a line that goes out into 3D space

59
00:02:30.719 --> 00:02:35.490
that starts at our player's center and has an end point.

60
00:02:35.490 --> 00:02:37.409
And we were gonna use this to determine

61
00:02:37.409 --> 00:02:39.490
if we are looking at a light switch or not.

62
00:02:39.490 --> 00:02:42.129
So here's a breakdown of the nodes

63
00:02:42.129 --> 00:02:43.030
that we're gonna be using.

64
00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:45.370
So we're gonna use our input action interact

65
00:02:45.370 --> 00:02:46.830
as our trigger.

66
00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:47.810
Then what we're gonna do

67
00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:50.650
is we're gonna use a combination of our get actor location,

68
00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:53.930
our get controlled pawn and our get actor forward vector

69
00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:56.729
to determine the location and the rotation

70
00:02:56.729 --> 00:02:59.490
that the player is currently facing in the world.

71
00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:00.689
And we're gonna use that

72
00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:05.180
inside of our line trace by channel node.

73
00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:06.139
And we're gonna use this

74
00:03:06.139 --> 00:03:09.139
to give us a start and an ending value.

75
00:03:09.139 --> 00:03:10.280
And once we've done that,

76
00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:12.939
we can then do things off of our out hit,

77
00:03:12.939 --> 00:03:15.039
which we'll describe here in just a little bit.

78
00:03:15.039 --> 00:03:20.039
So let's go ahead and come over to the editor now.

79
00:03:20.199 --> 00:03:22.520
And we're gonna come over to our event graph

80
00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:24.639
and let's go ahead and start adding stuff.

81
00:03:24.639 --> 00:03:25.639
So first things first,

82
00:03:25.639 --> 00:03:28.479
we're gonna look for our IA underscore

83
00:03:28.479 --> 00:03:30.960
and look at that, we have our IA interact.

84
00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:33.599
So that's the first thing that we want right there.

85
00:03:33.599 --> 00:03:38.319
All right, so then we're gonna look for our get actor

86
00:03:38.319 --> 00:03:39.879
and we probably gonna have to disable

